### What the bot found (5/5 deliberate defects)

| Line | Severity | Finding |
|------|----------|---------|
| 4 | critical | Hardcoded admin password in source code |
| 8 | critical | MD5 used for password hashing (cryptographically broken) |
| 13 | critical | Command injection — user input concatenated into a shell command |
| 18 | major | Unbounded recursion on negative input → stack overflow / DoS |
| 23 | major | Assignment (`=`) instead of comparison (`===`) in `if` — always true |

---

## Architecture (final)

```
PR opened/synchronized
  └─> GitHub webhook (HMAC-SHA256 verified)
        └─> Vercel function /api/webhook
              ├─ build app JWT (RS256, private key)
              ├─ exchange for installation access token (cached 1h)
              ├─ fetch PR files + diff  (installation token)
              ├─ review in parallel with NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra
              └─ POST check run with inline annotations (installation token)
```

---

## Bugs found and fixed during bring-up

| # | Symptom | Root cause | Fix |
|---|---------|-----------|-----|
| 1 | Every webhook returned **401** | Env vars set via Windows `echo` carried a trailing `\r`; the HMAC secret never matched | Re-set all Vercel env vars from files instead of `echo` |
| 2 | No `pull_request` events ever delivered | Installation had **0 repositories** granted and `permissions: {}` | User accepted the pending permission update, granted the repo |
| 3 | Handler returned **500** | `const { owner, repo } = repository` — the payload exposes `repository.name`, not `.repo` | Destructure `name` instead |
| 4 | Check run rejected **403 "You must authenticate via a GitHub App"** | Bot used a user token; the Checks API requires an installation token | Added `app-auth.ts`: app JWT → installation token |
| 5 | Function **timed out at 60s** (Vercel Hobby cap) | Sequential per-file model calls, unbounded prompt and token budget | Parallel file review, 3-file cap, 12k-char prompt cap, 35s per-call timeout, 45s wall budget |

---

## Secrets involved (all must be rotated)

| Secret | Where used |
|--------|-----------|
| GitHub App private key | `GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY` (Vercel) |
| GitHub App ID `5127527` | `GITHUB_APP_ID` (Vercel) |
| Webhook secret | `GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (Vercel + app settings) |
| NVIDIA API key | `NVIDIA_API_KEY` (Vercel) — used for the model calls |
| GitHub tokens | `GITHUB_TOKEN` (obsolete now) + classic PAT used for setup |

The bot no longer needs a user token: installation tokens are minted per request.

---

## Constraints discovered

- **Vercel Hobby caps a function at 60s.** A plan upgrade to Pro (300s) would remove the
  file-count and prompt caps and allow reviewing whole PRs.
- **Free-tier NVIDIA endpoints are variable.** Latency ranged 1s → 30s+ for the same
  prompt. Retries and fallbacks matter more than raw model choice.
- **Checks API is app-only.** Any future feature that posts to a PR must use the
  installation token, never a PAT.

